  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Georgia Strait - Production and Flux Observations, 1995-1999",
  "description": "Observations of physical, biological, sedimentation and chemical parameters in Georgia Strait, 1995-1999.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Seasonal cycles of particulate flux out of surface waters, primary production; physical and chemical properties of Haro Strait and Juan de Fuca Strait; nutrient supply/export mechanisms; Euphausiid distribution and stock assessment.\n\nSupplemental information: Risk Justification: Data are in electronic format, well backed up and well documented. Risk of Loss: Low Impact Justification: Time series of 5 to 10 years Impact of Loss: Medium Recommended Action: None Additional Info: Other researchers collaborated in these cruises: Coring in the Strait of Georgia for tracer and contaminant concentrations (R. Macdonald, MEHS, IOS), Tests of CTD-turbulence probe (A. Gargett, OSAP, IOS). The isotope ratios were determined at UBC.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23570694",
